GPIO_TC_001	gpio_reg_wr_rd_test	GPIO Register Write/Read Test - Verifies default reset values of all GPIO GP0 registers (gp0_gpio_8 to gp0_gpio_39, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1, gp0_intr2_intr_sts1, gpio_io_ctrl_group1-4, gpio_dout_group1-4, gpio_din_group1-4) and performs write-read-back verification with multiple data patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000) using write_mask and read_mask arrays. Validates that RO fields cannot be written and WO fields cannot be read.	GPIO	GPIO0 (GP0)	Register Access	Default Value Check; Write-Read Verification	Register	P1 - High	1. System reset (hreset_n) applied.
2. GPIO0 instance selected (#define GPIO0 1).
3. CNT=49 registers configured in addr_array.	1. Apply system reset.
2. Read all 49 GPIO registers and compare against default_value_array (mask with 0xFFFFFFFE for data_in bit).
3. Skip registers marked in skip_rst_array.
4. Skip non-readable registers (read_mask=0x00000000).
5. Write pattern 0xFFFFFFFF (masked with write_mask_array) to all writable registers.
6. Read back and verify: expected = (write_data & read_mask & write_mask) | (~write_mask & read_mask & default_value).
7. Repeat steps 5-6 for patterns: 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000.
8. Skip registers marked in skip_array for write/read.	1. All register default values match default_value_array after reset.
2. All write-read-back values match expected computed values for each pattern.
3. def_fail_cnt = 0 and wr_fail_cnt = 0.
4. finish(0) called indicating PASS.	gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10, gp0_gpio_11, gp0_gpio_12, gp0_gpio_13, gp0_gpio_14, gp0_gpio_15, gp0_gpio_16, gp0_gpio_17, gp0_gpio_18, gp0_gpio_19, gp0_gpio_20, gp0_gpio_21, gp0_gpio_22, gp0_gpio_23, gp0_gpio_24, gp0_gpio_25, gp0_gpio_26, gp0_gpio_27, gp0_gpio_28, gp0_gpio_29, gp0_gpio_30, gp0_gpio_31, gp0_gpio_32, gp0_gpio_33, gp0_gpio_34, gp0_gpio_35, gp0_gpio_36, gp0_gpio_37, gp0_gpio_38, gp0_gpio_39, gpio_intr_raw_stclr1, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, gp0_intr2_intr_en1, gp0_intr2_intr_sts1, gpio_io_ctrl_group1, gpio_io_ctrl_group2, gpio_io_ctrl_group3, gpio_io_ctrl_group4, gpio_dout_group1, gpio_dout_group2, gpio_dout_group3, gpio_dout_group4, gpio_din_group1, gpio_din_group2, gpio_din_group3, gpio_din_group4	0x00, 0x04, 0x08, 0x0C, 0x10, 0x14, 0x18, 0x1C, 0x20, 0x24, 0x28, 0x2C, 0x30, 0x34, 0x38, 0x3C, 0x40, 0x44, 0x48, 0x4C, 0x50, 0x54, 0x58, 0x5C, 0x60, 0x64, 0x68, 0x6C, 0x70, 0x74, 0x78, 0x7C, 0x80, 0x84, 0x88, 0x8C, 0x90, 0x94, 0x98, 0x9C, 0xA0, 0xA4, 0xA8, 0xAC, 0xB0, 0xB4, 0xB8, 0xBC, 0xC0	data_in[0], intr_raw_sts[1], intr_clr[16], pedge_intr_en[17], nedge_intr_en[18], level_sel[19], io_ctrl[20], dout[21]; G8-G39_intr_raw_stclr[0:31]; G8-G39_intr_en[0:31]; G8-G39_intr_sts[0:31]; G8-G39_io_ctrl[0:7]+wr_mask[16:23]; G8-G39_dout[0:7]+wr_mask[16:23]; G8-G39_din[0:7]	data_in: RO; intr_raw_sts: RO; intr_clr: WO; pedge_intr_en: RW; nedge_intr_en: RW; level_sel: RW; io_ctrl: RW2; dout: RW2; gpio_intr_raw_stclr1: VRRW; gp0_intr1_intr_en1: RW; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1: RO; gpio_io_ctrl_group: VRRW; gpio_dout_group: VRRW; gpio_din_group: RO	io_ctrl default=1 (input mode); all others default=0	Per write_mask_array[49] - defines writable bits per register	Per read_mask_array[49] - defines readable bits per register	GPIO0=1; CNT=49; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 through MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_39; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_x_DEFAULT_VAL; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_x_READ_MASK; GPIO_GP0_GPIO_x_WRITE_MASK	program.c, test_define.c	TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test/	NA	NA	NA	def_fail_cnt=0 AND wr_fail_cnt=0; finish(0) called	def_fail_cnt>0 OR wr_fail_cnt>0; finish(1) called	Registers at offsets 0x80,0x94,0x98,0x9C,0xA0,0xA4,0xA8,0xAC,0xB0 (VRRW type) are skipped for write/read via skip_array. Registers at offsets 0x94-0xC0 are skipped for reset value check via skip_rst_array. data_in bit masked with 0xFFFFFFFE during default value comparison.
GPIO_TC_002	test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en	GPIO Level-Select Interrupt Enable Test - Validates GPIO level-triggered interrupt generation for all 32 GPIO pins (GPIO_8 to GPIO_39). Tests both active-high level (level_sel=1, io_ctrl=input mode, bit19=1 & bit20=1 => 0x00180000) and active-low level (level_sel=0, io_ctrl=input mode, bit20=1 => 0x00100000) interrupt modes. Verifies GIC IRQ routing (IRQ 87 for GPIO0), group interrupt enable/status via gp0_intr1_intr_en1/gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, individual interrupt raw status via gp0_gpio_x[1], interrupt clear via gp0_gpio_x[16], and sysreg interrupt status clear via LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1.	GPIO	GPIO0 (GP0)	Interrupt	Level-Select Interrupt; Active-High Level; Active-Low Level; GIC IRQ Handling; Group Interrupt; Sysreg Interrupt	Functional	P1 - High	1. System reset (hreset_n) applied.
2. GPIO0 instance selected (#define GPIO0 1).
3. GIC configured and enabled.
4. LSS SYSREG accessible.	1. Enable GIC IRQ 87 for GPIO0.
2. Enable sysreg interrupt: write LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1.
3. ACTIVE-HIGH LEVEL TEST (loop i=0 to 31):
   a. Write 0x00180000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) to set input mode + level_sel=1.
   b. Wait 50 cycles.
   c. Enable group interrupt: write (1<<i) to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 (offset 0x84).
   d. Write 0xFFFFFFFF to SRAM (0xA0243FFC) to drive GPIO pin high.
   e. Wait for interrupt (int_pend loop).
   f. In ISR: verify intr_raw_sts bit[1] is set; verify group interrupt status bit[i] in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 (offset 0x88).
   g. Clear interrupt: write 0x00110000 to GPIO register (bit16=1 for intr_clr).
   h. Verify cleared: read GPIO register, expect 0x100001.
   i. Disable group interrupt: write 0x0 to INTR_EN1.
   j. Verify group status cleared.
   k. Clear sysreg: write LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR to MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1.
   l. Verify sysreg status cleared.
   m. Clear GIC IRQ 87.
4. ACTIVE-LOW LEVEL TEST (loop i=0 to 31):
   a. Write 0x00100000 to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4) to set input mode + level_sel=0.
   b. Wait 50 cycles.
   c. Enable group interrupt: write (1<<i) to INTR_EN1.
   d. Write ~(1<<i) to SRAM to drive GPIO pin low.
   e. Wait for interrupt and repeat ISR verification as above.
5. Call finish(test_err).	1. For each GPIO pin (8-39), interrupt raw status bit[1] is set when level condition is met.
2. Group interrupt status bit[i] is set in gp0_intr1_intr_sts1.
3. After interrupt clear (write bit16=1), GPIO register reads 0x100001.
4. Group interrupt status clears to 0x0 after disabling INTR_EN1.
5. Sysreg RAW_STCR1 GPIO0_INTR bit clears after write.
6. All 32 pins pass for both active-high and active-low levels.
7. test_err=0; finish(0) called.	gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_39, gp0_intr1_intr_en1, gp0_intr1_intr_sts1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1	0x00-0x7C (GPIO_8 to GPIO_39), 0x84 (INTR_EN1), 0x88 (INTR_STS1), LSS_SYSREG offsets: INTR_EN1=0x28, RAW_STCR1=0x24	data_in[0], intr_raw_sts[1], intr_clr[16], pedge_intr_en[17], nedge_intr_en[18], level_sel[19], io_ctrl[20], dout[21]; G8-G39_intr_en[0:31]; G8-G39_intr_sts[0:31]; gpio0_intr[1] in SYSREG_INTR_EN1/RAW_STCR1	data_in: RO; intr_raw_sts: RO; intr_clr: WO; level_sel: RW; io_ctrl: RW2; gp0_intr1_intr_en1: RW; gp0_intr1_intr_sts1: RO; SYSREG_INTR_EN1: INTREN1; SYSREG_RAW_STCR1: RAWSTCR1	io_ctrl default=1; level_sel default=0; all interrupt enables default=0; all interrupt status default=0	GPIO register write_mask per spec; INTR_EN1 fully writable [31:0]	GPIO register read_mask per spec; INTR_STS1 fully readable [31:0]	GPIO0=1; GIC_EnableIRQ(87); GIC_ClearIRQ(87); MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1; MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1; LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1_GPIO0_INTR; LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1_GPIO0_INTR	program.c, test_define.c	TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_level_sel_intr_en/	87 (GPIO0); 88 (GPIO1)	MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1 (offset 0x24); MIZAR_LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1 (offset 0x28)	gpio0_intr (bit 1 in RAW_STCR1/INTR_EN1)	test_err=0; finish(0) called; All 32 GPIO pins pass interrupt generation and clearing for both active-high and active-low levels	test_err>0; finish(test_err) called with non-zero; Any GPIO pin fails interrupt raw status check, group interrupt check, interrupt clear check, or sysreg status clear check	Test uses SRAM location 0xA0243FFC to drive GPIO input values. Active-high: writes 0xFFFFFFFF. Active-low: writes ~(1<<i). ISR handler (Default_IRQHandler) performs all verification. GPIO0 uses GIC IRQ 87; GPIO1 uses GIC IRQ 88 (conditional compilation). Level interrupt: bit19=level_sel, bit20=io_ctrl(input mode). Interrupt clear: write 1 to bit16 (intr_clr).